   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "shouldn't we only compare the pubkey? What if some metadata such as depth, fingerprint, etc. is missing (or is 0)? They key still a valid key but we would silently omit it.",
   "request": "Compare only pubkeys rather than all metadata (depth, fingerprint) to avoid omitting valid keys from other wallets",
   "status": "answered",
   "status_by": {
    "at": "2026-09-30",
    "by": "achow101",
    "id": "rc:4147697210",
    "quote": "I think we want to be as specific as possible here to avoid any unexpected surprises."
   },
   "status_note": "author explained that specificity avoids surprises when visually different xpubs get private keys",
